1
00:01:30,530 --> 00:01:34,970
[AWAKEN]

2
00:01:35,539 --> 00:01:37,930
[Episode 22]

3
00:01:49,789 --> 00:01:51,039
Go get Mika.

4
00:01:51,330 --> 00:01:51,850
Yes.

5
00:01:52,950 --> 00:01:53,789
And...

6
00:01:55,870 --> 00:01:56,590
Yoshiko.

7
00:02:09,759 --> 00:02:10,430
Over there!

8
00:02:10,449 --> 00:02:10,979
Yes!

9
00:02:24,690 --> 00:02:27,450
How did the water bottle break?

10
00:02:28,850 --> 00:02:31,180
I accidentally knocked it to the floor.

11
00:02:32,560 --> 00:02:33,240
Mr. Hoshino.

12
00:02:33,240 --> 00:02:34,870
Wait here for a moment.

13
00:02:36,240 --> 00:02:36,970
Mr. Hoshino,

14
00:02:37,470 --> 00:02:40,079
it's so good that you've recovered.

15
00:02:49,030 --> 00:02:49,750
Mika.

16
00:02:51,910 --> 00:02:53,750
What did you put in the matcha?

17
00:02:55,100 --> 00:02:57,579
I only put a little bit of honey.

18
00:02:58,800 --> 00:03:00,800
Why did you do that?

19
00:03:02,360 --> 00:03:04,080
Matcha is too bitter for me,

20
00:03:04,510 --> 00:03:08,030
so I usually add some honey to flavor it.

21
00:03:11,790 --> 00:03:16,280
Don't you know there's pollen in honey?

22
00:03:17,560 --> 00:03:18,310
Mr. Hoshino,

23
00:03:18,890 --> 00:03:21,520
I didn't know you were allergic to pollen.

24
00:03:22,710 --> 00:03:23,960
I'm really sorry.

25
00:03:29,280 --> 00:03:31,000
Your explanation is perfect.

26
00:03:38,470 --> 00:03:39,200
Mr. Hoshino.

27
00:03:45,980 --> 00:03:51,610
Someone warned me before
that there was a mole in the lab,

28
00:03:52,600 --> 00:03:54,670
but I didn't believe it.

29
00:03:57,520 --> 00:04:04,240
After all,
I brought you all here from Japan.

30
00:04:05,390 --> 00:04:06,230
But today,

31
00:04:06,840 --> 00:04:08,670
after I left,

32
00:04:09,750 --> 00:04:11,150
someone snuck in,

33
00:04:11,860 --> 00:04:15,570
stole experimental sample No. 369,

34
00:04:16,890 --> 00:04:19,209
and switched the lab mouse.

35
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:25,290
Only you two stayed here today.

36
00:04:26,930 --> 00:04:28,170
Who did it?

37
00:04:37,040 --> 00:04:43,800
My beloved students always disappoint me.

38
00:04:47,450 --> 00:04:48,260
Where are we going?

39
00:04:48,260 --> 00:04:49,390
Hoshino Institute.

40
00:04:49,570 --> 00:04:50,840
They caught two spies,

41
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:53,000
and they want us to go identify them.

42
00:04:54,159 --> 00:04:55,490
NBIS or the Communists?

43
00:04:56,159 --> 00:04:57,820
You'll know when we get there.

44
00:05:10,680 --> 00:05:11,560
Dr. Hoshino.

45
00:05:13,050 --> 00:05:16,290
Good thing you warned me.

46
00:05:17,410 --> 00:05:18,670
I almost got deceived.

47
00:05:19,750 --> 00:05:21,480
I actually thought

48
00:05:21,870 --> 00:05:23,120
there was only one

49
00:05:24,600 --> 00:05:26,270
disobedient dog.

50
00:05:39,950 --> 00:05:41,040
Miss Shen?

51
00:05:42,950 --> 00:05:44,070
It's you?

52
00:05:47,950 --> 00:05:48,560
Kailai,

53
00:05:49,400 --> 00:05:51,260
you should believe me now, right?

54
00:05:51,720 --> 00:05:53,480
I didn't kill Miss Shen.

55
00:06:03,160 --> 00:06:04,630
I really admire you.

56
00:06:05,560 --> 00:06:06,910
You actually managed

57
00:06:07,040 --> 00:06:09,120
to infiltrate Dr. Hoshino's lab.

58
00:06:11,510 --> 00:06:13,160
I'd like to know

59
00:06:13,250 --> 00:06:15,640
how you got in.

60
00:06:23,870 --> 00:06:24,720
Dr. Hoshino.

61
00:06:25,830 --> 00:06:27,800
One of them is a Communist,

62
00:06:27,950 --> 00:06:29,410
and the other is from NBIS.

63
00:06:30,040 --> 00:06:32,300
Let me take them back for interrogation.

64
00:06:32,560 --> 00:06:35,360
I will definitely give you
a satisfactory answer.

65
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:38,659
Interrogate them right here.

66
00:06:40,510 --> 00:06:44,990
Until I find my beloved little animal,

67
00:06:46,630 --> 00:06:48,560
no one leaves.

68
00:07:05,360 --> 00:07:07,090
Since neither of you will talk,

69
00:07:08,560 --> 00:07:10,420
please forgive me for being rude.

70
00:08:08,410 --> 00:08:12,240
Where did you hide the lab mouse?

71
00:08:16,980 --> 00:08:18,420
I really don't know.

72
00:08:34,730 --> 00:08:36,210
Do you?

73
00:08:45,030 --> 00:08:46,000
Stupid!

74
00:08:47,830 --> 00:08:50,200
I'm giving you a chance to live.

75
00:08:51,190 --> 00:08:54,240
I can search every corner.

76
00:08:55,200 --> 00:08:55,910
By then,

77
00:08:56,480 --> 00:08:58,560
neither of you will be alive.

78
00:09:03,030 --> 00:09:03,840
Dr. Hoshino,

79
00:09:05,240 --> 00:09:07,270
these two are very stubborn.

80
00:09:07,290 --> 00:09:08,620
They won't talk easily.

81
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:10,840
However,

82
00:09:11,390 --> 00:09:13,480
I know a very interesting game.

83
00:09:14,550 --> 00:09:16,600
I wonder if you'd like to try it.

84
00:09:20,720 --> 00:09:21,390
What is it?

85
00:09:26,920 --> 00:09:28,400
If only one of them

86
00:09:28,820 --> 00:09:29,950
can live,

87
00:09:31,630 --> 00:09:32,960
will we

88
00:09:33,070 --> 00:09:34,670
hear more truth?

89
00:09:40,670 --> 00:09:41,930
Between the two of you,

90
00:09:42,030 --> 00:09:43,360
whoever confesses more

91
00:09:43,480 --> 00:09:44,750
is the winner.

92
00:09:46,360 --> 00:09:47,360
For the winner,

93
00:09:47,870 --> 00:09:50,320
I'll treat her
to a big bowl of sweet soy milk

94
00:09:50,320 --> 00:09:52,980
from Dahuchun Pan-fried Bun
tomorrow morning.

95
00:09:54,750 --> 00:09:56,720
And whoever loses,

96
00:09:58,120 --> 00:09:59,960
I'll dissect her

97
00:10:01,440 --> 00:10:06,200
and use her to replace my Subject No. 369.

98
00:10:09,790 --> 00:10:10,910
It's settled then.

99
00:10:16,360 --> 00:10:17,910
Who goes first?

100
00:10:27,030 --> 00:10:27,720
I will.

101
00:10:30,480 --> 00:10:32,680
At the door, I saw her sneak into the lab.

102
00:10:35,980 --> 00:10:36,740
She's lying.

103
00:10:39,080 --> 00:10:41,540
She knew Mr. Hoshino
was allergic to pollen.

104
00:10:41,720 --> 00:10:43,920
She deliberately added honey to the tea

105
00:10:44,140 --> 00:10:45,300
and took the opportunity
to steal the sample.

106
00:10:45,300 --> 00:10:46,160
I know nothing.

107
00:11:04,550 --> 00:11:05,600
Cowards.

108
00:11:07,240 --> 00:11:10,000
You're both cowards.

109
00:11:33,930 --> 00:11:37,010
This is my favorite piece.

110
00:11:39,630 --> 00:11:41,320
You're a good student.

111
00:11:41,870 --> 00:11:45,320
You must have done
a lot of research on me.

112
00:12:05,550 --> 00:12:06,510
Miss Shen,

113
00:12:09,120 --> 00:12:10,720
it was you, right?

114
00:12:11,200 --> 00:12:12,130
I didn't take it.

115
00:12:13,090 --> 00:12:14,490
I knocked out Mr. Hoshino

116
00:12:14,970 --> 00:12:16,260
to cover her escape.

117
00:12:21,030 --> 00:12:21,630
Is that so?

118
00:12:22,720 --> 00:12:23,360
No.

119
00:12:24,840 --> 00:12:26,840
I really don't know where No. 369 is.

120
00:12:28,640 --> 00:12:30,500
But I can tell you something else.

121
00:12:30,900 --> 00:12:34,210
The NBIS's most secret gathering place
in Shanghai

122
00:12:34,920 --> 00:12:36,580
is the Shikumen at Qiufengdu.

123
00:12:38,670 --> 00:12:40,550
They live right in your old room.

124
00:12:46,750 --> 00:12:47,680
Interesting.

125
00:12:49,510 --> 00:12:51,670
NBIS's imagination in choosing a hideout

126
00:12:51,670 --> 00:12:52,440
is truly...

127
00:12:53,600 --> 00:12:54,960
extraordinary.

128
00:12:59,480 --> 00:13:01,270
I will report
to General Kagesa immediately

129
00:13:01,270 --> 00:13:02,730
and prepare for a roundup.

130
00:13:08,790 --> 00:13:09,720
Miss Shen.

131
00:13:12,840 --> 00:13:14,410
I almost believed her.

132
00:13:19,510 --> 00:13:20,970
The so-called NBIS hideout

133
00:13:20,970 --> 00:13:22,480
is just a deceptive trick.

134
00:13:23,800 --> 00:13:25,110
If you go there now,

135
00:13:27,320 --> 00:13:29,050
you will instead alert the NBIS

136
00:13:29,150 --> 00:13:32,410
that their hidden agent in the institute
has been exposed.

137
00:13:39,700 --> 00:13:41,280
During the Battle of Nanjing,

138
00:13:41,280 --> 00:13:42,480
I learned Morse code.

139
00:13:43,500 --> 00:13:44,310
That's great.

140
00:13:44,630 --> 00:13:46,290
You must memorize these well.

141
00:13:46,670 --> 00:13:47,720
This notebook

142
00:13:49,460 --> 00:13:51,100
contains some letters,

143
00:13:51,270 --> 00:13:52,360
numbers,

144
00:13:53,320 --> 00:13:54,600
and symbols.

145
00:14:01,030 --> 00:14:01,720
Very well.

146
00:14:03,780 --> 00:14:05,310
Thank you for the reminder.

147
00:14:05,670 --> 00:14:06,550
However...

148
00:14:07,720 --> 00:14:10,120
what are you tapping out
with your fingers?

149
00:14:12,790 --> 00:14:14,150
It's Morse code.

150
00:14:16,440 --> 00:14:18,300
She is passing information to me,

151
00:14:18,440 --> 00:14:20,440
telling me where the item is hidden.

152
00:14:24,390 --> 00:14:25,790
Tell me where the item is.

153
00:14:28,840 --> 00:14:31,080
The sample is hidden in the dorm.

154
00:14:32,270 --> 00:14:33,000
She said

155
00:14:34,120 --> 00:14:35,250
the one who survives

156
00:14:35,510 --> 00:14:36,770
must take the item out.

157
00:14:37,910 --> 00:14:38,770
You sold me out.

158
00:14:39,960 --> 00:14:41,620
They won't let you off even so!

159
00:14:44,390 --> 00:14:45,000
Search.

160
00:14:57,390 --> 00:14:58,670
Search everywhere thoroughly.

161
00:14:58,670 --> 00:14:59,790
Don't miss a single corner.

162
00:14:59,790 --> 00:15:00,750
Yes!

163
00:15:07,600 --> 00:15:08,870
You, search this room.

164
00:15:09,270 --> 00:15:09,870
Yes.

165
00:15:14,910 --> 00:15:15,840
You, that room.

166
00:15:15,840 --> 00:15:16,900
Search over there!

167
00:15:23,200 --> 00:15:24,150
Miss Shen.

168
00:15:25,670 --> 00:15:27,240
For Kailai's sake,

169
00:15:27,240 --> 00:15:29,040
I originally wanted to save you.

170
00:15:29,600 --> 00:15:30,440
But...

171
00:15:31,550 --> 00:15:32,960
you failed me.

172
00:15:33,490 --> 00:15:36,550
Battalion Commander Du, you were once
a soldier who fought for the country,

173
00:15:36,550 --> 00:15:39,010
but now you've become
a dog for the Japanese.

174
00:15:40,390 --> 00:15:42,200
The civilians and soldiers
who died in Nanjing—

175
00:15:42,200 --> 00:15:44,030
if they saw you today—

176
00:15:44,670 --> 00:15:47,470
I wonder what they would think
in the netherworld!

177
00:15:51,480 --> 00:15:53,210
No one has the right to judge me!

178
00:15:53,720 --> 00:15:54,550
No one!

179
00:16:42,440 --> 00:16:43,300
What happened?

180
00:16:44,200 --> 00:16:45,200
Dr. Hoshino!

181
00:16:45,760 --> 00:16:46,410
Doctor!

182
00:16:46,440 --> 00:16:47,170
Dr. Hoshino!

183
00:16:47,630 --> 00:16:48,480
Come help!

184
00:16:48,790 --> 00:16:49,480
Hurry!

185
00:16:50,960 --> 00:16:52,220
Doctor, hang in there!

186
00:16:52,850 --> 00:16:53,730
Let's go!

187
00:17:16,200 --> 00:17:16,960
Mr.

188
00:17:19,369 --> 00:17:20,300
I am truly sorry.

189
00:17:20,500 --> 00:17:22,740
How could Hoshino die?

190
00:17:22,760 --> 00:17:23,720
I am truly sorry!

191
00:17:25,280 --> 00:17:30,170
You couldn't even protect Hoshino
with so many people?

192
00:17:31,180 --> 00:17:33,860
We were tricked.

193
00:17:34,200 --> 00:17:35,400
Fools!

194
00:17:41,230 --> 00:17:42,880
Did you find the sample?

195
00:17:44,190 --> 00:17:46,050
We searched the dorm thoroughly,

196
00:17:48,270 --> 00:17:49,680
but only found this.

197
00:17:56,010 --> 00:17:58,290
Those two women never left.

198
00:18:00,070 --> 00:18:02,790
The sample couldn't have flown away
by itself!

199
00:18:04,980 --> 00:18:10,430
Not even a single thread
can leave the lab!

200
00:18:10,680 --> 00:18:13,680
Yes, the institute
is completely locked down.

201
00:18:13,920 --> 00:18:16,190
Our men are still searching.

202
00:18:22,410 --> 00:18:25,040
You killed them
without getting any answers?

203
00:18:26,110 --> 00:18:27,840
Is this what you are capable of?

204
00:18:29,830 --> 00:18:31,400
It's my incompetence.

205
00:18:34,420 --> 00:18:38,350
If the sample really falls into the hands
of the Communists or the NBIS,

206
00:18:38,550 --> 00:18:41,310
we will all have to answer to the Emperor.

207
00:18:49,770 --> 00:18:52,330
Was there anyone else

208
00:18:52,360 --> 00:18:54,740
who entered or left
the institute at that time?

209
00:18:54,740 --> 00:18:57,740
No one else except us.

210
00:19:09,920 --> 00:19:11,650
What about that photographer?

211
00:19:40,340 --> 00:19:41,380
After you go back,

212
00:19:41,480 --> 00:19:43,030
you must practice repeatedly.

213
00:19:43,030 --> 00:19:44,720
In an emergency,

214
00:19:44,790 --> 00:19:45,550
Morse code

215
00:19:45,550 --> 00:19:47,680
is the most covert way to communicate.

216
00:20:02,400 --> 00:20:03,310
A photographer

217
00:20:04,110 --> 00:20:06,510
should capture
all the beauty in the world.

218
00:20:07,890 --> 00:20:09,950
But what is the most beautiful thing?

219
00:20:17,480 --> 00:20:18,740
Hello, Broken Bridge.

220
00:20:19,440 --> 00:20:20,370
I'm Su Causeway.

221
00:20:38,510 --> 00:20:40,040
If I leave and never return,

222
00:20:41,440 --> 00:20:42,720
then so be it.

223
00:20:46,000 --> 00:20:47,260
The future is unknown.

224
00:20:49,000 --> 00:20:50,800
I will remember you as you are now

225
00:20:51,240 --> 00:20:52,770
and think of you as you were.

226
00:21:16,480 --> 00:21:17,200
Xin Xiang!

227
00:21:19,880 --> 00:21:21,010
We've been exposed.

228
00:21:21,200 --> 00:21:22,200
Go buy 2 boat tickets.

229
00:21:22,200 --> 00:21:22,790
Hurry up!

230
00:21:23,050 --> 00:21:23,620
Where to?

231
00:21:23,650 --> 00:21:25,050
Anywhere is fine! Go now!

232
00:21:27,820 --> 00:21:29,080
Wait for me at the pier.

233
00:21:29,270 --> 00:21:30,270
If I don't show up,

234
00:21:30,680 --> 00:21:31,740
leave by yourself.

235
00:21:50,270 --> 00:21:50,880
Hello.

236
00:21:51,140 --> 00:21:52,540
Su Causeway passed away.

237
00:21:52,590 --> 00:21:54,520
I put the sample in the usual place.

238
00:22:02,400 --> 00:22:03,200
Where are you?

239
00:22:03,750 --> 00:22:04,750
The photo studio.

240
00:22:05,550 --> 00:22:07,110
Why did you go back to the photo studio?

241
00:22:07,110 --> 00:22:08,570
My negatives are all here.

242
00:22:09,110 --> 00:22:10,030
They are all I have.

243
00:22:10,030 --> 00:22:11,490
I can't leave them behind.

244
00:22:11,660 --> 00:22:12,880
That's very dangerous.

245
00:22:12,880 --> 00:22:13,510
Leave now!

246
00:22:14,090 --> 00:22:15,550
See you at the usual place.

247
00:22:29,910 --> 00:22:31,040
Where are you going?

248
00:22:54,480 --> 00:22:55,440
Jinbao is dead.

249
00:22:57,350 --> 00:22:59,480
I can't keep running the photo studio.

250
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:01,600
It's time for me to leave too.

251
00:23:03,160 --> 00:23:04,050
You can go.

252
00:23:05,680 --> 00:23:07,210
But leave the thing behind.

253
00:23:08,600 --> 00:23:09,360
What thing?

254
00:23:12,400 --> 00:23:13,860
Stop playing dumb with me.

255
00:23:15,640 --> 00:23:17,480
That little animal we lost

256
00:23:17,640 --> 00:23:18,840
is with you, isn't it?

257
00:23:24,070 --> 00:23:25,240
The Morse code

258
00:23:25,470 --> 00:23:27,080
Miss Shen tapped

259
00:23:28,030 --> 00:23:29,290
wasn't for that woman.

260
00:23:30,830 --> 00:23:31,830
It was for you.

261
00:23:34,350 --> 00:23:35,810
You think too highly of me.

262
00:23:37,790 --> 00:23:39,920
I actually underestimated you so much

263
00:23:41,350 --> 00:23:42,680
that I ignored

264
00:23:43,010 --> 00:23:44,670
the flaws you showed long ago.

265
00:23:46,680 --> 00:23:48,200
If you were from the NBIS,

266
00:23:48,200 --> 00:23:49,480
that would make sense,

267
00:23:50,000 --> 00:23:52,570
because you've always been with
the God of Wealth.

268
00:23:52,570 --> 00:23:53,230
However...

269
00:23:55,200 --> 00:23:57,730
even the God of Wealth
couldn't have imagined

270
00:23:59,000 --> 00:24:01,000
that you were actually a Communist.

271
00:24:12,870 --> 00:24:14,150
I always remember

272
00:24:15,200 --> 00:24:16,880
you saved me at Fairy Bath.

273
00:24:18,140 --> 00:24:18,860
So,

274
00:24:20,640 --> 00:24:22,770
as long as you give the thing back to me,

275
00:24:23,960 --> 00:24:24,960
I'll let you go.

276
00:24:27,720 --> 00:24:28,720
And we two

277
00:24:29,110 --> 00:24:30,710
will owe each other nothing.

278
00:24:38,030 --> 00:24:39,120
Can I trust you?

279
00:24:42,510 --> 00:24:43,750
Do you have a choice?

280
00:24:47,880 --> 00:24:48,590
Alright.

281
00:24:59,640 --> 00:25:00,200
Good!

282
00:25:01,200 --> 00:25:02,110
That's right!

283
00:25:03,030 --> 00:25:03,920
Promising.

284
00:25:04,880 --> 00:25:05,750
In these times,

285
00:25:07,120 --> 00:25:08,640
only guns work!

286
00:25:14,110 --> 00:25:14,720
Good!

287
00:25:15,240 --> 00:25:15,960
Keep going!

288
00:25:42,000 --> 00:25:43,510
I gave you your gun.

289
00:25:45,330 --> 00:25:46,860
I taught you marksmanship.

290
00:25:48,350 --> 00:25:50,790
The M1910 only holds six rounds.

291
00:25:51,270 --> 00:25:52,270
There's only

292
00:25:53,070 --> 00:25:55,070
an empty magazine in your gun now.

293
00:25:58,330 --> 00:25:58,930
Come on.

294
00:26:00,070 --> 00:26:01,030
Shoot me.

295
00:26:04,190 --> 00:26:05,350
Shoot me!

296
00:26:22,000 --> 00:26:22,880
I told you,

297
00:26:24,000 --> 00:26:25,070
I am your mentor.

298
00:26:26,590 --> 00:26:27,750
You can't beat me.

299
00:26:37,890 --> 00:26:38,720
Just give up.

300
00:26:41,590 --> 00:26:42,750
I won't give up.

301
00:26:44,640 --> 00:26:46,240
I only care about the result.

302
00:26:47,480 --> 00:26:48,240
If you lose,

303
00:26:48,880 --> 00:26:49,920
you lose.

304
00:26:51,270 --> 00:26:53,070
I only care about the result too.

305
00:26:54,680 --> 00:26:55,480
In the end,

306
00:26:57,110 --> 00:26:58,880
my faith will definitely win.

307
00:26:59,110 --> 00:27:00,270
Faith? My foot!

308
00:27:02,070 --> 00:27:03,200
Give me the thing.

309
00:27:05,590 --> 00:27:07,390
I've already sent the thing out.

310
00:27:08,640 --> 00:27:09,270
Now,

311
00:27:10,470 --> 00:27:11,930
I have nothing but my life.

312
00:27:14,790 --> 00:27:15,550
Stupid!

313
00:27:27,400 --> 00:27:28,000
Come on.

314
00:27:29,480 --> 00:27:31,740
Raise the camera hanging from your chest

315
00:27:32,610 --> 00:27:34,340
and take another picture of me.

316
00:27:35,070 --> 00:27:36,790
Make me look macho,

317
00:27:37,830 --> 00:27:40,760
because this might be the last picture
you ever take.

318
00:29:03,400 --> 00:29:05,400
This is called a spring-loaded gun.

319
00:29:06,880 --> 00:29:09,070
Jinbao saw it in a detective magazine.

320
00:29:12,030 --> 00:29:13,030
This camera

321
00:29:15,520 --> 00:29:16,850
was left by my master.

322
00:29:19,580 --> 00:29:21,380
I've always had only one master.

323
00:29:23,720 --> 00:29:24,980
His name is Li Musheng.

324
00:29:26,410 --> 00:29:27,520
A year ago today,

325
00:29:29,110 --> 00:29:31,110
he died at the hands of the Japanese.

326
00:29:32,430 --> 00:29:34,590
Are you trying to rebuild a camera?

327
00:29:35,400 --> 00:29:36,730
If you had that ability,

328
00:29:37,000 --> 00:29:38,830
you wouldn't even need
to be a photographer.

329
00:29:38,830 --> 00:29:41,230
You might as well
find a shop on Nanjing Road

330
00:29:41,270 --> 00:29:42,510
and sell cameras.

331
00:30:05,410 --> 00:30:07,610
A camera has never been useless.

332
00:30:10,240 --> 00:30:11,440
It is my weapon.

333
00:30:13,160 --> 00:30:14,270
Always has been.

334
00:31:59,930 --> 00:32:01,040
For this sample,

335
00:32:02,000 --> 00:32:03,860
Su Causeway sacrificed herself.

336
00:32:05,640 --> 00:32:08,640
With the latest experimental sample
of Project Slumber,

337
00:32:08,640 --> 00:32:10,360
we can cultivate antibodies

338
00:32:10,890 --> 00:32:12,610
and save more lives.

339
00:32:16,400 --> 00:32:17,730
I know about the sample.

340
00:32:18,400 --> 00:32:19,680
What is the film for?

341
00:32:22,110 --> 00:32:22,910
The codebook.

342
00:32:23,900 --> 00:32:25,830
The codebook for Project Slumber.

343
00:32:27,640 --> 00:32:28,830
NBIS previously obtained

344
00:32:28,830 --> 00:32:30,830
some encrypted experimental data,

345
00:32:31,110 --> 00:32:32,770
but they couldn't decrypt it.

346
00:32:33,400 --> 00:32:35,600
This time, we finally got the codebook,

347
00:32:36,830 --> 00:32:38,690
but they sacrificed themselves.

348
00:32:38,790 --> 00:32:41,160
You helped them complete the mission.

349
00:32:49,830 --> 00:32:50,760
I didn't even...

350
00:32:53,510 --> 00:32:54,840
have a chance to hug her.

351
00:33:00,350 --> 00:33:01,550
Comrade Chen Kailai,

352
00:33:03,720 --> 00:33:05,450
you completed this operation,

353
00:33:06,550 --> 00:33:09,010
ensuring their sacrifices weren't in vain.

354
00:33:16,440 --> 00:33:17,900
Then where am I going next?

355
00:33:23,000 --> 00:33:23,800
To Chongqing.

356
00:33:25,200 --> 00:33:25,930
Chongqing?

357
00:33:28,110 --> 00:33:29,640
The superiors have decided

358
00:33:29,790 --> 00:33:31,880
that you will continue to stay undercover.

359
00:33:31,880 --> 00:33:34,010
Your codename remains Broken Bridge.

360
00:33:42,110 --> 00:33:42,960
Take this

361
00:33:44,640 --> 00:33:46,500
and give it to Jinbao's superior.

362
00:33:46,920 --> 00:33:48,580
Xin Xiang will take you there.

363
00:33:50,400 --> 00:33:51,350
He's one of us?

364
00:33:53,100 --> 00:33:54,300
He is from Chongqing.

365
00:34:01,440 --> 00:34:02,500
Will we meet again?

366
00:34:08,030 --> 00:34:08,630
We will.

367
00:34:09,800 --> 00:34:10,550
In Yan'an?

368
00:34:15,719 --> 00:34:16,550
I hope so.

369
00:35:10,590 --> 00:35:11,590
Jinbao

370
00:35:12,800 --> 00:35:14,130
loved wontons the most.

371
00:35:21,190 --> 00:35:22,150
Why are you here?

372
00:35:24,880 --> 00:35:26,110
Today is my birthday.

373
00:35:30,510 --> 00:35:32,840
When exactly is Jinbao's birthday?

374
00:35:37,110 --> 00:35:38,240
I don't know either.

375
00:35:42,000 --> 00:35:44,530
She gave me the codebook
for Project Slumber.

376
00:35:46,280 --> 00:35:48,140
I need to deliver it to Chongqing.

377
00:36:12,730 --> 00:36:13,730
Mr. Chen Kailai

378
00:36:13,960 --> 00:36:15,030
played a key role in helping

379
00:36:15,030 --> 00:36:16,760
the Party-State

380
00:36:16,800 --> 00:36:18,200
obtain Project Slumber.

381
00:36:19,000 --> 00:36:23,400
He has been specially approved to
officially join the Second Division of NBIS.

382
00:36:43,800 --> 00:36:45,000
Comrade Chen Kailai,

383
00:36:45,400 --> 00:36:47,660
the superiors have officially approved

384
00:36:47,760 --> 00:36:49,090
your party membership.

385
00:36:53,230 --> 00:36:54,360
I solemnly swear...

386
00:36:54,960 --> 00:36:56,090
I solemnly swear...

387
00:36:56,320 --> 00:36:59,320
That I volunteer to join
the Communist Party of China.

388
00:37:00,150 --> 00:37:03,150
That I volunteer to join
the Communist Party of China.

389
00:37:16,040 --> 00:37:18,740
[1943, Second Division of NBIS]

390
00:37:33,840 --> 00:37:36,580
[Li Moqun, Head of Agent 76,
Dies of Food Poisoning]

391
00:37:41,430 --> 00:37:42,570
I'm just afraid you won't get used to it.

392
00:37:42,570 --> 00:37:43,430
How could I not?

393
00:38:01,510 --> 00:38:02,970
I saw an old acquaintance.

394
00:38:03,030 --> 00:38:05,190
He was my photographer at No. 76.

395
00:38:05,960 --> 00:38:07,090
What a coincidence.

396
00:38:07,820 --> 00:38:08,820
I'll go say hi.

397
00:38:23,550 --> 00:38:24,480
Long time no see.

398
00:38:25,510 --> 00:38:26,440
Long time no see.

399
00:38:29,950 --> 00:38:31,030
You look good.

400
00:38:32,670 --> 00:38:33,710
You too.

401
00:38:38,510 --> 00:38:39,630
If you hadn't taken that picture

402
00:38:39,630 --> 00:38:41,150
of me on the train,

403
00:38:42,750 --> 00:38:44,950
maybe none of this would have happened.

404
00:38:46,320 --> 00:38:47,110
Thank you

405
00:38:48,400 --> 00:38:50,930
for bringing me into
this complicated world.

406
00:38:56,030 --> 00:38:56,920
I have to go now.

407
00:39:00,150 --> 00:39:01,440
May I have this dance?

408
00:39:55,260 --> 00:40:00,080
[Early Spring, 1949]
[Nanjing, Ministry of Defense, BIS]

409
00:40:33,550 --> 00:40:35,510
It's a task
assigned personally by the Director.

410
00:40:35,510 --> 00:40:36,360
Pack your things

411
00:40:36,360 --> 00:40:38,020
and prepare to leave Nanjing.

412
00:40:38,070 --> 00:40:38,720
Where to?

413
00:40:39,190 --> 00:40:40,760
Qibao Town, Songjiang.

414
00:40:41,430 --> 00:40:42,150
To do what?

415
00:40:42,920 --> 00:40:43,710
Go dormant

416
00:40:44,460 --> 00:40:45,790
and wait to be awakened.

417
00:40:49,600 --> 00:40:54,430
[October 1, 1949, Chunguang Photo Studio]

418
00:40:52,000 --> 00:40:53,550
Compatriots!

419
00:40:55,230 --> 00:41:00,550
The Central People's Government

420
00:41:01,880 --> 00:41:05,000
of the People's Republic of China

421
00:41:05,960 --> 00:41:08,710
is established today!

422
00:41:28,500 --> 00:41:29,430
Long time no see.

423
00:41:29,800 --> 00:41:30,730
Long time no see.

424
00:41:43,420 --> 00:41:44,060
Thank you.

425
00:41:48,840 --> 00:41:51,860
I now work at
Shanghai Municipal Public Security Bureau.

426
00:41:51,860 --> 00:41:53,660
After the founding of New China,

427
00:41:54,230 --> 00:41:55,480
since on the surface

428
00:41:55,760 --> 00:41:57,400
you are a BIS agent

429
00:41:57,630 --> 00:41:58,890
codenamed Polar Bear,

430
00:42:01,230 --> 00:42:02,800
when Taiwan awakens you,

431
00:42:03,390 --> 00:42:05,230
that will be when we awaken you.

432
00:42:10,410 --> 00:42:13,860
[BIS, Taiwan]

433
00:42:14,640 --> 00:42:17,220
[File Card of BIS, Ministry of Defense,
Republic of China]

434
00:42:17,780 --> 00:42:20,740
[Chen Kailai]

435
00:42:28,610 --> 00:42:31,950
[1951]

436
00:42:57,230 --> 00:42:58,230
Polar Bear,

437
00:42:59,030 --> 00:43:00,920
please wake up from your hibernation.
